<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of La Ciudadela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1831">1831</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentine-civil-wars">Argentine Civil Wars</a> · <a href="/encyclopedia/wars">All wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of La Ciudadela was fought on 4 November 1831 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-miguel-de-tucuman">San Miguel de Tucumán</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-facundo-quiroga">Juan Facundo Quiroga</a>'s Federalist army defeated the Unitarian forces of Gregorio Aráoz de Lamadrid. The victory destroyed the League of the Interior, and the interior provinces joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-pact">Federal Pact</a>, completing the Federalist triumph in the civil war.</p></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Background</h2><p>The Unitarian League of the Interior had depended on the leadership of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-paz">José María Paz</a>, and when he was taken prisoner by the Federalists, Gregorio Aráoz de Lamadrid fell back with his army to Tucumán. There he reorganised a demoralised force of fewer than 1,500 men, repelled attacks from Salta Province and held off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-felipe-ibarra">Juan Felipe Ibarra</a> at Río Hondo, forcing him back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago-del-estero">Santiago del Estero</a>.</p><p>Facundo Quiroga, meanwhile, had regained power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuyo">Cuyo</a> with only 450 men, though rheumatism slowed him, and gathered in Mendoza a force of 1,200 cavalry and 500 infantry. His second in command, Bargas, was defeated by the Unitarians at Miraflores in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catamarca-province">Catamarca Province</a>, after which Quiroga took command himself and marched on Tucumán in pursuit of Lamadrid.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Course of events</h2><p>Fighting began at noon on 3 November at Famaillá, where thick forest held up the Federalists. The next morning, at the Citadel, Quiroga divided his army into two wings, the left under General José Ruiz Huidobro and the right under Martín Yanzón and Nazario Benavídez. Lamadrid's forces were commanded by Javier López and Juan Esteban Pedernera. For two hours neither side prevailed, and several times Lamadrid seemed close to winning, but Quiroga personally led each scattered regiment back into the fight. The obedience Quiroga commanded outweighed the greater numbers of the Tucumán forces; Lamadrid blamed the hesitation of some of his colonels, above all Pedernera.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Aftermath and significance</h2><p>The Federalists lost fewer than fifty dead, Bargas among them, while the Unitarians had over two hundred dead and more than a thousand taken prisoner; some 33 captured Unitarian officers were executed. Lamadrid and most of his officers fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salta">Salta</a>, whose government refused to raise a new army, and then to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>. On 2 December the governors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-rioja">La Rioja</a> and Salta signed a peace at Tucumán by which Salta undertook to follow federal policy and pay La Rioja's war costs. General Alejandro Heredia became governor of Tucumán, and the leading Tucumán Unitarians were made to pay <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-reparations">reparations</a> to Quiroga.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Battle of La Ciudadela” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Quiroga defeated the Unitarians at <b>La Ciudadela</b> near Tucumán in November 1831, and the provinces joined the Federal Pact, forming the Argentine Confederation.</blockquote><a href="/state/unitarian-league">Unitarian League</a></li></ul></section>
